---
description: >-
  Every swimlane label kind (lane title, node text and edge label) written
  the six ways of spec #1368: plain markdown, a quoted markdown string,
  bare backticks, a code span in plain text, the common tags and a written
  \n. Only the quoted markdown string reads markdown; the bare backticks
  and the code span are drawn as written, the tags draw and \n breaks the
  line. Each lane holds a node written the same way, and the edge into it
  too.
---
swimlane-beta LR
  subgraph L1[lane **bold** _ital_]
    A[node **bold** _ital_]
  end
  subgraph L2["`lane **bold** _ital_`"]
    B["`node **bold** _ital_`"]
  end
  subgraph L3[`lane **bold** _ital_`]
    C[`node **bold** _ital_`]
  end
  subgraph L4[lane a `code` b]
    D[node a `code` b]
  end
  subgraph L5[lane <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
    E[node <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
  end
  subgraph L6[lane one\ntwo]
    F[node one\ntwo]
  end
  A -->|edge **bold** _ital_| B
  B -->|"`edge **bold** _ital_`"| C
  C -->|`edge **bold** _ital_`| D
  D -->|edge a `code` b| E
  E -->|edge <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O| F
  F -->|edge one\ntwo| A
